      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the real numbers \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) that satisfy the given equation, consider the general form by completing the squares:\n\\[ x^2 - 10x + y^2 + 6y = -34 \\]\n\nWe complete the square for both \\( x \\) and \\( y \\):\n\nFor \\( x^2 - 10x \\):\n\\[ x^2 - 10x = (x-5)^2 - 25 \\]\n\nFor \\( y^2 + 6y \\):\n\\[ y^2 + 6y = (y+3)^2 - 9 \\]\n\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[ (x-5)^2 - 25 + (y+3)^2 - 9 = -34 \\]\n\nSimplifying, we combine constants on the right side:\n\\[ (x-5)^2 + (y+3)^2 - 34 = -34 \\]\n\\[ (x-5)^2 + (y+3)^2 = 0 \\]\n\nSince both squares are nonnegative and equal to zero:\n\\[ (x-5)^2 = 0 \\]\n\\[ (y+3)^2 = 0 \\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[ x-5 = 0 \\]\n\\[ y+3 = 0 \\]\n\nSolving these:\n\\[ x = 5 \\]\n\\[ y = -3 \\]\n\nFinally, the desired value is:\n\\[ x + y = 5 + (-3) = 2 \\]\n\nSo, the answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2} \\]",
